# Editors and agent tooling
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json
.idea/
*.swp

# Agent/assistant working directory. Its contents are machine-specific: a
# launch config pointing at a local dev server, local permission grants, and
# session scratch. None of it describes the project, and a launch config that
# hard-codes one machine's port or path is actively misleading to check in.
# Ignored wholesale rather than per-file, with one deliberate exception: if a
# genuinely shared, reviewed agent config is ever wanted, un-ignore that single
# file the way .vscode/extensions.json is un-ignored above, so the shared part
# is an explicit, reviewable opt-in and the local part stays out.
.claude/

# OS junk
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Never commit user data.
#
# Workout Conductor is local-first: real training history lives in the browser's
# IndexedDB and belongs to the person using the app, not to this repository.
# Exported backups, restored history, and hand-made "just for testing" dumps all
# contain personal data. Test fixtures must be synthetic and explicitly named as
# fixtures; anything matching the patterns below is blocked outright.
#
# npm run privacy:scan enforces the same rule in CI. If a file you need is being
# ignored here, rename the fixture rather than loosening these lines.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.backup.json
workout-history*.json
/backups/
/private/
*.user.json
